football hall of famer who knows a thing  or two about the tampa bay buccaneers  getting to the super bowl and winning it  he was a cornerstone of the team that  did it 18 years ago super bowl 37  champion  derek brooks joining us derek how are  you  pal doing all right mike and yourself  oh i'm doing great and and i just  noticed as the shot came up if there's  ever a shortage of footballs in the  world you will make a lot of money  oh man oh my god don't thank me my wife  she  uh found all these balls that i  collected and she kind of put together  this thing behind me so uh  i pretty much kept every uh interception  of test down uh that i was involved in i  kept the ball and  uh she found him and this was she got  set up behind me  oh it looks awesome she did a great job  what's the one ball that you would never  part with  oh uh i would say  all of them but probably the  interception for touchdown is superbowl  37 that's  that is one that uh  i really i had to keep close to my arm  after that game  i mean i didn't let it go i didn't trust  the equipment manager with it  i didn't trust family  i kept that ball the whole time so i  would probably say that's the one  uh i would not part ways  you're on the host committee for this  super bowl how different is this super  bowl just the fact that fans aren't  going to be there like they normally  would the media is not there like that  like it normally is and how unfortunate  is this for for tampa the city of tampa  which you know wanted this super bowl  and now has it but it's going to be so  different  well serene i was i would say that we're  not taking the attitude of it's  unfortunate we're  taking the attitude that we're taking  advantage of everything that we do have  and we do have a great game that we're  celebrating with our team the bucks  celebrating the first part of history by  getting here  uh it's going to be enough people  watching and participating that's  rooting them on to be a part of this now  obviously things have changed when it  comes to the media and your guys  covering the game and you've uh and your  colleagues have had to make that  transition all year long so we look at  this as you guys are used to doing this  in this same space and place we just  want to make sure you guys continue to  have all the access points that you've  had in previous years when it comes to  a super bowl now yes we've had to  rewrite the blueprint no doubt about it  everything that we've learned the past  few years  we've had to throw half of it out  and pivot and make audibles and  adjustments to  make sure that everything involving  safety and healthcare and protocols are  first and foremost  in all of our fans uh lives  and we're still having some of familiar  events we just scaled back obviously the  number of participants when you have to  limit the capacity so we've tried to  keep all the fan experience things in  we just have to reduce the amount of  access in terms of fans being able to  attend  so uh yes we hopefully we set the stage  for the cities that's coming behind us  that they don't have to start from zero  like we did  hey derek when you played for the  buccaneers you made number 55 legendary  there's now a linebacker on the team  wearing number 45. when you see devin  white what is your reaction  uh explosive play maker  you can see he's getting even more  comfortable in his in this defense which  is taking advantage of his skill set  obviously they drafted him where they  drafted him to be a playmaker and an  impact player and devon has done that at  the same time mike i do have to  recognize the young man beside him  lavontay david and i think levonte has  been  one of  probably the most consistent players for  a long time in this league that hasn't  gotten the attention and i think levante  and him playing together do a good job  of complementing each other's skill set  so i really like to think that levonte  has built into the development of devon  white but devin white has definitely  come on and shown that he's ready to be  the leader of that defense  derek you guys won with defense back in  your day and this team is so much more  on on offense but if you had to draw up  a game plan to stop patrick mahomes what  would you do how would you stop him  well irene i know you got some problems  from kansas city people watching this  thing so i don't want to get away  [Laughter]  you know some some conversations that i  may or may not have had  but i'll say this here's here's what  they can do if you go back and look  obviously at the raiders and even last  year's super bowl there's a formula  there that teams have had success with  and  the books  but believe it or not it can be a very  similar in terms of their game plan yes  you're gonna have to uh offensively  you're gonna have to help your defense  when you're playing patrick mahomes in  this offense by having a consistent  running game that eats up clock  defensively  they've done a good job of getting  turnovers in the playoffs so they've got  hot at the right time and creating  pressure in creating turnovers and with  patrick and his offense with kansas city  gives you an opportunity to get a  turnover you have to take advantage of  it meaning if you're going up for an  interception you got to come down with  the ball it can't be a fast breakup when  you have him corralled in the pocket you  have to bring him down do not let him  extend plays and escape and make the  plays using his god given ability that  he's made and creating uncomfortable  pocket and lastly i will say this  they have to take away kansas city's  running game  that is how kansas city got back in the  super bowl last year against san  francisco by running the football and  creating an opportunity for downfield  passing plays and they did a great job  of that at green bay and taking away the  running game from aaron rodgers and  obviously when they were able to do it  they made plays against aaron  defensively so  i would say very similar game plans  obviously different skill sets when it  comes to these teams but that to me is  is a pathway of success when you're  going against an explosive offense and  at the end of the day you make it a  physical football game  derek the buccaneers were seven and five  going into a week 13 bye week they're  7-0 cents then the offense gets so much  of the attention i think we overlook  collectively how much better the defense  has gotten where have you seen the most  improvement on the defensive side of the  ball the past seven games  uh they've got healthier and you go back  to the second half of that atlanta game  that defense came out the second half  and they've been on a roll as i said  before whether it was creating pressure  and turnovers  to even scoring themselves in winning  the field position battle and that's  where i think  the tom brady experiment the tom brady  expertise in tampa  really showed up  when the bucks were seven and five and  struggling because they've been in  similar positions in the years past  and they've not won enough games to get  in the playoffs when they was reeling  down the stretch this year  i think tom being in the leadership  position was able to influence this team  keep this team together and they haven't  looked back since the second half for  that atlanta game that's why i think  again his experience has influenced the  entire football team but you're right  mike the defense you know as well as  they've been playing yes  you're going to give up yards in today's  game  but you play well  in the red zone and you create turnovers  in today's game that equals good defense  now obviously when i played that was  considered terrible if it's giving up  all those yards but in today's games the  offense is going to get yards you just  do what you can to prevent them from  scoring in the red zone and when you  have an opportunity to get a turnover  you have to get turnovers  derek we talk a lot about the tampa two  defense you and warren sapp off that  defense or in the hall of fame maybe  it's the tampa three different defense  after this year  your buddy john lynch is is up for the  hall of fame again a finalist and i've  presented him a couple times now uh and  so is ira kaufman from from the tampa  bay area but what would it mean for john  lynch to go into the hall of fame in  tampa with you guys it would be pretty  special wouldn't it  yes at first i do want to thank you for  you know  taking my phone calls and listening to  every year you're listening to my  political speech as i make an argument  in a case with john  and even rondae and simeon so again  thank you for  uh really asking a question and seeking  information  but how fitting would that be if john or  rondae was able to get in  the team is playing and making history  at least by playing in the super bowl  it's super bowl 55 which always has a  special ring to it personally but to see  my good friends one of them you know one  of them get in  you know it's just a little bit more  than icing on the cake obviously john  has been waiting the longest uh of any  of the finalists  and i think obviously he's deserving of  that  honor years ago so i hope this year is  the year in rendez  uh by getting in that top 10 you never  know what happens but i do believe uh  with my heart of hearts and including  simeon rice that all three of them have  hall of fame resumes and deserve to join  warren and myself as well as  neighborhood sellman  as tampa bay buccaneer hall of famers  hey derek last one for you john gruden  was the coach of the team that won super  bowl 37  never got back with the bucks couple of  playoff appearances after that and now  three years in as raiders head coach  after a long break not able to get back  to the postseason do you see it turning  for gruden and him getting back to the  postseason on a regular basis with the  raiders  yes i do and i think each year mike  they've gotten a little bit better i  think john has adjusted  to his long layoff you know from the  league and saw that this is a different  league that he's come back to than when  he left and i think they made a good job  of that a good job of adjusting  you look at the changes he's made this  offseason on the coaching staff i'm very  impressed with this staff that he has  right now and i believe in it because i  know him and i believe in them that they  can get things turned around it doesn't  matter that they're in the same division  as kansas city because they showed  last year that they can not only play  with them but they can beat them so i  think the changes that john has made  he's finally got everything solidified  and now just again as he might continue  to uh adjust the personnel to the  schemes that they have i still think the  raiders can get back and they make an  even bigger jump next year  hey derek awesome stuff we appreciate  you we appreciate your time  congratulations on all your success and  all the best this week as we get ready  for super bowl 55.  uh congratulations to you guys and as  always it's fun seeing you on tv and  listening to you and you give my buddy  chris sims a break man you're really  hard on chris  i love chris  all right he makes it easy to be hard on  him thanks man take care that's derek  brooks hall of famer super bowl 37  champion  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

